# foldctl_2tier_64_h4_matched.topo -- the CONTROL baseline for the -rs_local_fold
# causal test (simulation-scripts/model_checks/fold_slack_test.py).
#
# 2-tier, 64 hosts, 4 hosts per leaf, full bisection, at the same primitives as
# scaleup_3tier_256_4000Gbps.topo: 4000 Gbps (= 2 ps/B), 50 ns link, 300 ns switch.
# Every link is therefore EXACTLY rate matched: four host links at 4000 feed a leaf
# that folds 4:1 and forwards on one 4000 Gbps uplink. Pair with the _up8000 sibling,
# which differs ONLY in the shared link's rate.
Nodes 64
Tiers 2
Podsize 64

Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 4000
Radix_Down 4
Radix_Up 4
Downlink_Latency_ns 50
Switch_Latency_ns 300
Oversubscribed 1

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 4000
Radix_Down 16
Downlink_Latency_ns 50
Switch_Latency_ns 300
